      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MEASURE AND EXPORT: numbers out of the graph\n\nEverything measured here already existed as an array; what was missing was a way OUT of it. Three nodes close that:\n\n  'CV Concat Arrays' (axis 1) glues the per-region columns into ONE table - box geometry from 'CV BBoxes To Array', area from 'Masks to BBoxes'. Axis 1 is side by side; axis 0 would have appended rows.\n\n  'CV Array To Text' formats the table as CSV/TSV/JSON. It has no file picker on purpose: wire it into 'Basic data handling: save STRING to file' to write a .csv, and into core 'Preview as Text' to read it here. 'Parse Matrix' is the return leg - this graph runs it in-place to prove the round trip, which is what a file would go through in a real run.\n\n  'CV Array To Numbers' / 'CV Numbers To Array' are the LIST bridge: the first emits a ComfyUI list of FLOATs, so basic_data_handling's sort / filter / min / max surface and an Inspire foreach can finally reach array values; the second collects them back. Keep the counts small - each value is a separate downstream execution.\n\nThe chart at the end is fed by the ROUND-TRIPPED table, not the original, so anything the text step loses would be visible."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
